WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — spellcheck (45s) Narrator Misha

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.362
First, people once paid hundreds of dollars for standalone spell check,

2
00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:07.867
yet today it comes free everywhere.

3
00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:11.856
Second, it became free because checking a word costs

4
00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:15.337
almost nothing to run inside tools you already use.

5
00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:20.425
Third, new computer intelligence reaches seven billion people only

6
00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:24.017
when it runs cheaply on devices people already own.

7
00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:30.933
In January 1981, an advertisement priced a personal-computer spell checker at two hundred dollars.

8
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:38.070
Nobody pays per typo today because clever dictionary compression made checking instant on your own keyboard.

9
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.171
Twenty-dollar cloud subscriptions serve the few who can rent data centers;

10
00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:49.470
shrinking computer intelligence to fit ordinary phones unlocks free universal bundling for billions.
